{
  "client": "Eglot",
  "source": "https://elpa.gnu.org/packages/eglot-1.24.tar (eglot-1.24/eglot.el: eglot-client-capabilities, eglot--connect, eglot-workspace-folders, eglot-initialization-options, eglot--accepted-formats)",
  "version": "1.24",
  "transcribed": "2026-09-23",
  "notes": "Transcribed from source, not captured from a running editor. Eglot 1.24 is the latest GNU ELPA release at transcription time. Runtime-dependent values chosen for a plain install with no extra packages and default customizations: eglot-documentation-renderer nil and markdown-mode not installed (gfm-view-mode unbound), so eglot--accepted-formats yields [\"plaintext\"] for hover.contentFormat, completionItem.documentationFormat and signatureInformation.documentationFormat (with markdown-mode installed it would be [\"markdown\", \"plaintext\"]); yasnippet not installed, so completionItem.snippetSupport is false; local (non-TRAMP) project, so workspace.didChangeWatchedFiles.dynamicRegistration is true; eglot-report-progress t (default), so window.workDoneProgress is true; no :initializationOptions initarg, so initializationOptions is the empty object. :json-false is rendered as false and eglot--{} as {}. clientInfo.version comes from package-get-version, which is folded to the package's Version header at compile time. Workspace fields: eglot sends rootPath (expand-file-name of default-directory, which in reality carries a trailing slash, e.g. /WORKSPACE/), rootUri (eglot-path-to-uri, trailing slash stripped) and workspaceFolders (project root plus project-external-roots, none by default; real folder name is abbreviate-file-name of the root directory, e.g. /WORKSPACE/ or ~/...). Placeholders /WORKSPACE and WORKSPACE are used here per fixture convention. processId is emacs-pid in reality; null here per fixture convention. No trace, locale or workDoneToken is sent.",
